  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: A</p>\n<p>A: - Component <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> follows a straight line through the origin, meaning <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> is directly proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span>, so it is an Ohmic conductor.<br/>- Component <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> is a curve where the gradient (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{I}{V}\"></span>) decreases as <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> increases. Since <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R = \\frac{V}{I}\"></span>, a decreasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{I}{V}\"></span> means an increasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{V}{I}\"></span>, so the resistance increases (typical of a filament lamp).</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph shows how the current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> varies with the potential difference <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> for two electrical components, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which row correctly describes the nature of component <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and the change in resistance of component <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> as <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> increases?</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Component <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span></th><th>Resistance of component <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td>A.</td><td>Ohmic</td><td>Increases</td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td>B.</td><td>Ohmic</td><td>Decreases</td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td>C.</td><td>Non-Ohmic</td><td>Increases</td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td>D.</td><td>Non-Ohmic</td><td>Decreases</td></tr></tbody></table>"
  },
